{"id":"cef2c9b0-4a3d-4c04-be22-ac7fe3b399d0","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1879bb2446693589","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/preview-windows.tsx","baseline":{"blob":"5e017fcc17dc6c8bad5adc08a678411b87ee1e99","start":4837,"end":5082},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","cascadeAt","(","opened",":","number",")",":","number","{","const","room","=","Math",".","min","(","window",".","innerWidth","-","WIDTH",",","window",".","innerHeight","-","HEIGHT","-","CASCADE",")","-","FIRST_AT",";","return","FIRST_AT","+","(","opened","%","Math",".","max","(","FEWEST_PLACES",",","Math",".","floor","(","room","/","CASCADE",")","+","1",")",")","*","CASCADE",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"3dc071dcfb0862a9","after":"91f796f8936aefc1"}},"payload":{"text":"Where the `opened`th window opens: the cascade goes round again before a window would leave the page, as what's off the\npage stops being drawn (xterm's rendering pauses, for one) and can't be reached. (`CASCADE` of room kept for the title\nbar.) On a page too small for a whole window, still `FEWEST_PLACES`, so none opens exactly over the last.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:44:00.869Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:44:00.869Z"}
